cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >-
  If you use this software in academic work, please cite the version
  of the repository used in your study.

type: software

title: "Lattice-QFT-Quantum-Simulation"

authors:
  - given-names: "Oscar"
    family-names: "Vicente Blázquez"

abstract: >-
  A modular research framework for the quantum simulation of lattice
  quantum field theories and gauge models using variational and
  circuit-based quantum algorithms. The current reference implementation
  focuses on the Schwinger model in 1+1-dimensional lattice quantum
  electrodynamics and includes variational vacuum preparation,
  real-time Suzuki-Trotter evolution, configurable quantum quenches,
  modular physical observables, uncertainty analysis, ansatz
  benchmarking and reproducible research workflows.

version: "0.1.0"

date-released: "2026-08-04"

repository-code: "https://github.com/oscar-vbl/Lattice-QFT-Quantum-Simulation"

url: "https://github.com/oscar-vbl/Lattice-QFT-Quantum-Simulation"

license: "MIT"

keywords:
  - "quantum simulation"
  - "lattice quantum field theory"
  - "lattice gauge theory"
  - "Schwinger model"
  - "quantum electrodynamics"
  - "variational quantum algorithms"
  - "quantum computing"
  - "Qiskit"
  - "real-time quantum dynamics"
  - "vacuum persistence"
  - "Suzuki-Trotter evolution"
  - "research software"